1.188:
They are in search of the things below the earth.
Strepsiades.
Then they are searching for roots. Do not, then, trouble yourselves about this;

1.1499:
(from within). You will destroy us! You will destroy us!
Strepsiades.
For I also wish this very thing;

1.187:
How so?
Pisthetaerus
The air is between earth and heaven. When we want to go to Delphi, we ask the Boeotians for leave of passage;

1.1542:
Ah! then she is a sort of general manageress to the god.
Prometheus
Yes, precisely. If he gives you her for your wife, yours will be the almighty power. That is what I have come to tell you;
